date-released: "2026-06-12"
version: "1.1.0"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a pre-registered phenome-wide Mendelian
  randomization study of amyloid-PET cortical deposition against 1,574
  FinnGen R12 disease endpoints (N=500,348). The phenome-wide scan is
  instrument-limited: outside APOE the conservative panel resolves to
  three instruments (effectively the CR1 variant rs6656401), and a
  per-phecode statistical-power floor shows the scan detects only large
  effects (median minimum detectable odds ratio approx 2.8 at the
  within-panel Bonferroni threshold). The signal that survives is the
  previously-known CR1 locus, where genetically-predicted amyloid, AD
  risk, and brain-cortical CR1 expression share a causal variant for
  late-onset AD-spectrum dementia (Brain_Cortex coloc.abf PP.H4 = 0.98),
  a shared-variant result that is method- and prior-dependent (coloc.susie
  disagrees) and that does not establish amyloid mediation (reverse-direction
  MR is itself significant). This release (v1.1.0) supersedes the
  colocalisation numbers of earlier releases: it corrects a colocalisation-input
  artefact in which coloc.abf run on GTEx significant-pairs eQTL data,
  summarised as a maximum posterior across tissues, inflated false-positive
  colocalisation at the tight-LD CR1 locus (all 16 coloc-tested phecodes,
  including a forearm-fracture negative control, returned approx 0.98). Re-run
  with full-pairs eQTL data in the pre-specified Brain_Cortex tissue, the
  colocalisation is specific to the late-onset AD-spectrum phecodes and the
  negative control passes; a pre-specified 24-phenotype negative-control panel
  and a simulation on the real CR1 LD matrix bound the artefact (a known
  failure mode per Giambartolomei 2014 and Wallace 2021). A post-hoc ADNI
  tau-PET polygenic-score arm (n=218 EUR; OSF Amendment 5, model frozen
  pre-results) is reported as a coherence check. The deposit includes the
  locked 41-section pre-registration with 5 publicly-versioned amendments,
  the analytical pipeline (R + Python + bash; 30 R scripts including R/21
  power floor and empirical-null calibration, R/22 colocalisation-prior
  robustness, R/23 negative-control panel, R/24 full-pairs colocalisation
  regeneration, R/25 reverse-direction MR, R/27 significant-pairs-vs-full-pairs
  panel, R/28 truncation simulation, and R/29 Brain_Cortex-primary
  colocalisation), the per-panel instrument lists, the per-phecode results
  supplement as parquet + TSV + interactive HTML browser, per-stage MR result
  parquets, ADNI cascade group-level summary TSVs (no individual-level ADNI
  data per the Data Use Agreement), manuscript figures, and supplementary
  tables. Code is licensed MIT; derived data products are licensed CC-BY 4.0,
  see LICENSE file. Upstream summary-level GWAS data, individual-level ADNI
  data, and reference panels are not redistributed; canonical sources and
  SHA256 hashes are documented for re-download.
